## Context
Reviewed the generated RESEARCH output (which identified L05 Frontier Research / StageId.RESEARCH as the first unambiguous missing canonical layer and proposed three architectural candidate approaches) alongside the CRITIQUE output (which adversarially examined the latency coupling and synchronous blockings of these approaches).

## Synthesis & Decision
The adversarial critique accurately highlights that implementing L05 as a sequential stage (Candidate A) tightly couples planner throughput to research latency. However, introducing a "Robust Asynchronous Event and State Synchronization Layer" at this stage violates the strict canonical 19-layer sequence, which prioritizes completing the cognition pipeline (L05-L07, L09) before addressing asynchronous scaling.

Candidate A remains the most dependency-sound approach because it conforms to the existing `SoftLoop` execution model, preserving the working vertical slice (Construction Principle 1) and avoiding premature architectural abstraction. We will proceed with Candidate A (sequential instantiation of L05 RESEARCH into the `SoftLoop` planner loop) and acknowledge the critique by deferring asynchronous event decoupling until the cognition pipeline is complete.

